.TH GENERIC-PLAYER 1 "2026-11-01" "Generic Player 1.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
generic-player \- play music and videos with an audio visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B generic-player
.RI [ OPTION ]
.RI [ SOURCE ...]
.br
.B generic-player \-\-
.RI [ SOURCE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Generic Player
is a graphical music and video player for Linux desktops. It provides a
searchable queue, album artwork, shuffle, repeat, seeking, playback speed,
a sleep timer and optional lyrics and desktop media controls.
.PP
Each
.I SOURCE
may be a media filename, directory, JSON/M3U/M3U8 playlist, local
.B file:
URL, or direct HTTP/HTTPS media stream URL. Quote paths containing spaces.
Local file URLs must refer to an absolute path on this computer. Directories
are scanned for supported media files; nested directory symlinks are not followed.
.PP
Sources are added to the restored queue. Starting the application or opening
files does not start playback automatically; select a track and press Play.
An ordinary web page is not necessarily a playable media stream.
.PP
Spectrum and waveform views use decoded audio. Qt 6.8 or newer with the
FFmpeg backend supports audio-buffer visualization; Qt5 requires backend
audio-probe support. Playback remains available when visualization is
unsupported. Actual media formats depend on the installed codecs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing. Use this before filenames beginning with a hyphen.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the player:
.PP
.nf
generic-player
.fi
.PP
Add a local album and a playlist:
.PP
.nf
generic-player "$HOME/Music/Favorite Album" "$HOME/Music/mix.m3u8"
.fi
.PP
Add a local file URL:
.PP
.nf
generic-player "file:///home/alex/Music/Track%20One.flac"
.fi
.PP
Add a filename beginning with a hyphen:
.PP
.nf
generic-player \-\- \-track.mp3
.fi
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B P / Space / Alt+P
Play or pause. P and Space remain playback controls when a player button,
closed noneditable selector, or read-only lyrics view has focus.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right
Previous or next track.
.TP
.B Left / Right
Seek backward or forward five seconds.
.TP
.B M / S / R
Mute, toggle shuffle, or cycle repeat mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Focus queue search.
.TP
.B Escape in queue search
Clear the filter and return focus to the queue.
.TP
.B Enter on a focused button
Activate that button.
.TP
.B F11 / Escape
Enter fullscreen or return to the previous window state.
.TP
.B F1
Show all keyboard shortcuts.
.PP
Typing controls, editable selectors, dialogs, and open menus keep their normal
keys. Arrow keys retain their normal selector, slider, and text-navigation
behavior. Dedicated media keys can control playback while typing.
Fullscreen focuses the media view and restores the previous control on return.
.SH DESKTOP MEDIA CONTROLS
Generic Player publishes MPRIS through QtDBus on the desktop session bus.
The primary service name is
.BR org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.Generic_Player .
Additional instances append
.BR .instance<PID> .
The optional
.B playerctl
client can query metadata and control playback:
.PP
.nf
playerctl \-\-list\-all
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player play
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player pause
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player play\-pause
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player stop
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player next
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player previous
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player position 5+
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player volume 0.7
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player loop Playlist
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player shuffle On
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player metadata artist title
playerctl \-\-player=Generic_Player metadata generic\-player:year
.fi
.PP
Next and previous preserve paused or stopped playback when sent through MPRIS.
The tagged date is exposed as
.BR xesam:contentCreated ,
preserving its known precision. Unknown dates and years are omitted.
.SH OPTIONAL SONG NOTIFICATIONS
Choose
.B View > Song notifications
to select Automatic, Off, Desktop notifications (GNOME / KDE), Wayland OSD,
or Custom command. Automatic is the default for new preferences; existing
saved choices, including Off, are preserved. Artist, song and known year
are shown when the song changes; play, pause and stop update the status.
.PP
Automatic prioritizes an explicit GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_ARGV adapter, then an
explicit GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_SOCKET or GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_COMMAND override.
Without overrides, it tries a running compatible Wayland socket, an active
desktop notification service, and then a verified installed Wayland client.
Invalid explicit overrides are reported without silently switching services.
.PP
Desktop notifications use an already-running
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
service. This supports GNOME Shell, KDE Plasma, dunst, swaync and other
implementations of that protocol, without guessing from the desktop name.
They request a 5000 millisecond display; the service controls the actual
duration, appearance and Do Not Disturb policy. GNOME and KDE's private
volume or brightness overlays have separate access and timing restrictions;
song cards use their public desktop notification interface instead.
.PP
Wayland_OSD discovery checks compatible user-owned sockets in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR,
/run/user/<uid>, and /tmp/wayland-volume-osd-<uid>. Renaming the upstream
executable does not change its socket name, wayland-volume-osd.sock.
Client discovery checks
.BR osd ,
.BR wayland-osd ,
.BR wayland_osd ,
and
.B wayland-volume-osd
in /usr/bin, /usr/local/bin and PATH. The command's help must identify the
supported CLI before the normal media client starts or reuses its shared
daemon. Incompatible candidates are skipped. An initial artist/title card
may appear briefly before the complete song card replaces it.
No OSD package is installed and no configuration is changed.
.PP
A newly started compatible daemon receives a 5000 millisecond timeout.
For an already-running daemon, run
.B /usr/bin/osd setup
(or
use the actual executable name, such as
.BR "wayland-osd setup" )
and set
.B Hide timeout (ms)
to
.BR 5000 .
This setting applies to every card from that daemon, including volume cards.
There is no per-card timeout override in the current upstream protocol.
.PP
Custom command uses the explicit GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_ARGV adapter described
below. An arbitrary command's arguments cannot be inferred from its name.
A custom service that implements the public notification protocol is found
automatically; a compatible JSON socket can be configured explicitly.
.PP
After fixing an installation or starting its service, choose
.B View > Song notifications > Retry current song notification
or reselect the active mode. This retries the current song without requiring
a track change. Turning notifications Off cancels pending delivery work;
the shared OSD daemon may remain available to other applications.
.PP
Bind media keys directly to the playerctl commands above to avoid the OSD's
own media wrappers replacing the complete card with artist/title-only text.
An OSD is never required for installation, local playback, or MPRIS control.
Other MPRIS listeners can consume metadata and state signals independently.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/generic-player
Installed application code. The command launcher uses this location
independently of the current working directory.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/generic-player
Default launcher installed by
.BR "make install" .
The Debian package uses
.I /usr/bin/generic-player
instead.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share
Default prefix for the desktop entry, hicolor icon, man page and AppStream
metadata installed from source. The Debian package uses
.IR /usr/share .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/generic_player/session.json
Saved queue, playback position and preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/generic_player/theme.json
Saved color theme. If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the configuration base directory is
.IR ~/.config .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENERIC_PLAYER_QT_API
Set to
.B 5
or
.B 6
to select the Qt binding explicitly. If unset, the player selects an
available supported binding.
.TP
.B GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_COMMAND
One absolute path to a compatible Wayland_OSD client, such as /usr/bin/osd.
The value is not a shell command and must not include arguments. Quote paths
containing spaces. An invalid explicit override does not fall back to another
service. Automatic and Wayland OSD use this override when no compatible
socket can be reached, unless a higher-priority explicit adapter is selected.
.TP
.B GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_SOCKET
One absolute path to a user-owned Unix socket implementing the Wayland_OSD
newline-delimited JSON protocol. Automatic and Wayland OSD select only that
socket unless a higher-priority explicit argument adapter is selected.
The custom daemon must already be running; automatic client startup is
disabled for this override. An already-reachable socket needs no executable.
.TP
.B GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_ARGV
A JSON array of 1 to 32 strings, each at most 4096 characters, with at most
32768 characters of configuration.
The first item is a literal executable name on PATH or an absolute executable
path. Each remaining item is one argument; paths with spaces stay one item.
Automatic and Custom command use this adapter. Custom command requires it.
Arguments may contain
.BR {artist} ,
.BR {title} ,
.BR {album} ,
.BR {year} ,
.BR {status} ,
.B {text}
(artist, title and known year), and
.B {timeout_ms}
(5000). Missing artist, album and year fields are empty. Use double braces,
{{ and }}, for literal braces. Unsupported fields, format specifications
and conversions are rejected.
Shell expansion, pipes, redirection and command substitution are not evaluated.
The selected tool controls display duration; choose a command that sends a card
and exits within three seconds. The player stops commands that exceed that
deadline.
.PP
For example, with notify-send already installed:
.PP
.nf
GENERIC_PLAYER_OSD_ARGV='["notify-send","-t","{timeout_ms}",
"--","{status}","{text}"]' generic-player
.fi
.PP
The built-in desktop notification integration does not require notify-send.
Explicitly empty or malformed OSD overrides are errors; unset an override to
restore automatic discovery. OSD configuration errors do not block playback.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Preferred runtime directory for the Wayland_OSD socket. Relative or malformed
paths are ignored; normal discovery also checks /run/user/<uid> and the
legacy /tmp/wayland-volume-osd-<uid> directory.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration base directory. Installation and uninstallation do not remove
the user's saved queue or preferences.
.SH SOURCE INSTALLATION
Manual installation supports Debian/Ubuntu, Arch Linux and conventional Fedora
using the distribution's runtime dependencies listed in README.md.
The install and uninstall helpers use Python's standard library and do not
invoke a package manager.
.PP
From a source checkout or an extracted release, install the system dependencies documented
in README.md, then run:
.PP
.nf
make check
sudo make install
.fi
.PP
The dependency check works in a checkout or an extracted source release.
Its optional OSD checks inspect files and configuration only; they do not
launch OSD commands, contact services, or require a running session bus.
.PP
Run
.B sudo make uninstall
from the source checkout to remove a manual installation. The installer
tracks owned files and preserves unrelated or locally modified files.
Use the same installation variables used at install time. A
.B DESTDIR
value stages installation into another root for inspection.
.PP
Build a Debian package as a normal user with
.BR "make deb" .
Use the system package manager to install or remove that package; manual
uninstallation does not remove a package-managed installation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Help and version commands exit with status 0. Invalid command-line options
or unsupported URL syntax exit with status 2. A normal graphical session
returns the Qt application exit status.
